{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T19:39:58.222Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"3e9f2d7e484a891c56382bae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ts-starter-relative-package-identity"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Support relative local packages with compiler-owned identities"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Follow-up to PR 154. A Program can resolve a relative declaration import without packageId even when it crosses a nested local package boundary. The checker now inventories manifest locations during copying, without reading names, and returns unsupported_project_shape for a loaded unknown boundary unless the compiler identifies the package or the solution includes its project config. This avoids synthetic resolution and metadata ancestry. Broader relative-package support needs a compiler-owned identity contract; ordinary local declarations, unused metadata, installed dependencies and referenced projects remain supported."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["compatibility","compiler-api","follow-up"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-27T19:39:58.222Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T19:39:58.222Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Obtain ownership from actual Program resolution data without synthetic imports or package metadata ancestry; retain current typed refusal until identity is available; preserve direct compiler diagnostics and exact installed layouts; include named, unnamed, nested and mts/cts/ts package fixtures"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"sdk-contracts.ts","scope":"project"},{"path":"test/sdk-api-review.test.ts","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"docs/sdk-contract-api-compatibility.md","scope":"project"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"41796deb07a3d4e35c72c963bd0a18267f6c066856dfe5b2c0e125ba6ef86cad","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1dda0919984adce9b81d0bb745f5c6828e0f832c841158e85c9863fb2193ca83"}
